\[
\mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}.
\]
The transformations give us the system of linear equations:
\begin{align*}
\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 9 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}, \quad
\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}.
\end{align*}
This becomes:
\begin{align*}
\begin{cases}
2a - b = 9 & (1) \\
2c - d = 3 & (2) \\
a - 3b = 7 & (3) \\
c - 3d = -1 & (4)
\end{cases}
\end{align*}
\end{think}
