\begin{cases}
2a - b = 9 & (1) \\
2c - d = 3 & (2) \\
a - 3b = 7 & (3) \\
c - 3d = -1 & (4)
\end{cases}
\end{align*}
Solving equation $(1)$ for $a$, we have $a = \frac{9 + b}{2}$. Solving equation $(3)$ for $a$ gives $a = 7 + 3b$. Substituting both expressions for $a$ into one another, we have $\frac{9 + b}{2} = 7 + 3b$, which simplifies to $b = 1$. Substituting back into either expression for $a$, we get $a = 5$. Doing the same for $c$ and $d$, we substitute $y = 2x + 1$ into $\mathbf{M}$ and let $x = y - 1$, we find that
